{"kind":"request","text":"Review the design note head 8759bbf4 on branch planner/pointing-claims-packages-20261027 (request 0e06e751). It replaces the earlier draft you approved at 880d9cdf (b5ef7b94), so this supersedes review request d009cc31: notes/2026-10-27-pointing-and-claims.md is deleted in this head and was never on main, and notes/2026-10-28-boundary-objects-in-use.md is the note. Hugh held the earlier draft, reviewed this one, and asked for it to go to review in its place.\n\nWhat it does: it starts from the use cases instead of from acts. Section 3 walks five cases at the level of what is on the table and who touches it (this workroom observed, then cases 01, 30, 20 and 10). Section 4 tables what every other case passes between parties and what stays outside the fold. Section 5 names seven view kinds an agent builds on demand (a table matching one document against another, a list with a column per party, a grid, a timeline, two versions of one text, a marked image, a brief). Sections 6 to 8 derive what the record must hold and what changes in the composed-views direction. Section 9 keeps the smallest mechanism from the earlier draft: a locator inside a document, three acts in platform:commons@1 (note, ratify, close; no reference act), the consent rule on party slots, recipes over hashes, item ends against party closings, four witnesses and four slices BO1 to BO4.\n\nPlease check: that the catalogue cases are read correctly in sections 3 to 5 (numbers and who decides, against docs/use-cases.md at a78e0981); that section 9 is consistent with sections 5 to 8 and with the contract (packages/contract/src/definition.ts) and the chat-composed views note; that the public-material rules hold (no comparisons, no product names, plain English); and the three conclusions at this exact head. Merges clean onto origin/main 229a7c5b; the diff against main is the one new file. Nothing was run.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1